      "title": "Marketing and the consumer guide",
      "narration": "Maryland adopted the NAIC long-term care model regulation in COMAR Title 31, Subtitle 14. Insurers must establish marketing procedures that prevent twisting, high-pressure tactics and cold lead advertising, and must assure that comparisons are fair and accurate. At or before application Theo must give Gloria the long-term care consumer guide, the shopper’s guide, and an outline of coverage that describes benefits, exclusions, renewability and premium increase history in a standard format, along with the disclosure titled Things You Should Know Before You Buy Long-Term Care Insurance. Advertising must be filed with the Commissioner.",
