      "title": "Contingent nonforfeiture",
      "text": "If an insurer raises premiums by more than a threshold percentage that depends on the insured’s age at issue, and the policyholder lets the policy lapse, Maryland requires a contingent nonforfeiture benefit: a paid-up policy with a shortened benefit period equal to the premiums paid, even if the insured declined the nonforfeiture option at purchase.",
      "example": "After a 60 percent rate increase, Gloria stops paying; she keeps a paid-up benefit equal to the premiums she paid over the years.",
